NNAAMMEE
       winicontoppm - convert a Windows .ico image into 1 or more PPM images


SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       wwiinniiccoonnttooppppmm  [--wwrriitteeaannddss] [--aalllliiccoonnss|--bbeessttqquuaall] [--mmuullttiippppmm] [--vveerrbboossee]
       [_i_c_o_n_f_i_l_e] [_p_p_m_d_e_s_t_f_i_l_e]


DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       This program is essentially obsolete; The newer wwiinniiccoonnttooppaamm is better.

       wwiinniiccoonnttooppppmm reads a Microsoft Windows .ico file and converts it to one
       or more PPMs.

       A  Windows  icon  contains one or more images, at different resolutions
       and color depths.   Each  image  has  an  'and'  mask,  which  contains
       transparancy data.

       By  default,  the  output  goes to Standard Output.  If you specify _p_p_‐
       _m_d_e_s_t_f_i_l_e, output goes into one or more files  named  as  follows.   If
       it's  just  one  file  (i.e.  you specify the --mmuullttiippppmm option or don't
       specify --aalllliiccoonnss), the file name is _p_p_m_d_e_s_t_f_i_l_e..ppppmm.  If it's multiple
       files, their file names are _p_p_m_d_e_s_t_f_i_l_e__11..ppppmm, _p_p_m_d_e_s_t_f_i_l_e__22..ppppmm, etc.

        When you specify the --wwrriitteeaannddss option, the file names above are modi‐
       fied to include the string xxoorr as in  _p_p_m_d_e_s_t_f_i_l_e__xxoorr..ppppmm  or  _p_p_m_d_e_s_t_‐
       _f_i_l_e__xxoorr__11..ppppmm.

       wwiinniiccoonnttooppppmm  can  convert .ico images with 1, 4, 8, 24, or 32 bits per
       pixel.  Before Netpbm 10.15 (April 2003), it could not  handle  24  and
       32.


OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       In  addition  to  the options common to all programs based on libnetpbm
       (most notably --qquuiieett, see
        Common Options ⟨index.html#commonoptions⟩ ),  wwiinniiccoonnttooppppmm  recognizes
       the following command line options:



       --wwrriitteeaannddss
              For  each icon written, also write the 'and' (transparancy) mask
              as a separate PBM file.  It's  name  is  of  the  form  _p_p_m_d_e_s_t_‐
              _f_i_l_e__aanndd..ppbbmm or _p_p_m_d_e_s_t_f_i_l_e__aanndd__11..ppbbmm.


       --aalllliiccoonnss
              Extract all images from the .ico file.

              If you specify neither this nor --bbeessttqquuaall, wwiinniiccoonnttooppppmm extracts
              the first image.


       --bbeessttqquuaall
              Extract only the best quality (largest, then highest bpp)  image
              from the .ico file.

              If you specify neither this nor --aalllliiccoonnss, wwiinniiccoonnttooppppmm extracts
              the first image.


       --mmuullttiippppmm
              Write all PPMs to a single file.




